{"id":"h257","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"science-physics","question":"A single-electron atom has the electron in the l = 2 state. The number of allowed values of the quantum number m_l is\nIs the correct answer \"4\"?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"For l = 2, m_l takes the values −2, −1, 0, +1, +2.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The number of allowed m_l values is 2l + 1 = 5.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The answer 4 might come from forgetting that m_l = 0 is allowed.","confidence":0.6,"lean":0.0,"theta":0.9425,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The answer 4 might come from confusing the count with 2l = 4.","confidence":0.6,"lean":0.0,"theta":0.9425,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"2l = 4 as a count, or a different counting convention, justifies the answer 4.","confidence":0.03,"lean":1,"theta":0.0471,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"The rule m_l = −l, ..., +l follows from the angular-momentum quantum mechanics that gives the spherical harmonics.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Zero is a valid value of m_l.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The count 2l + 1 is the same whether the atom has one electron or many.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The proposed answer of 4 is incorrect.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":-0.7,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":-0.9,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i